From a0ee687c5c3f837645092a5ee4e22bb43b915f4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:52:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] shell: quick launch on every two-button combo

Only Back+Up and Up+Down could be held together to launch an app, each
copied through prefs, the watchface and the app cache. Replace the two
with a table of all six pairs (adding Back+Select, Back+Down, Up+Select
and Select+Down), behind one QuickLaunchCombo API.

The existing qlComboBackUp and qlComboUpDown keys keep their names, so
bindings set from the phone carry over. The four new keys are writable
from the phone too.

Quick Launch settings on the watch gain a row per combo. The app menu
now edits a QuickLaunchBinding (hold, tap or combo) instead of a button
and a tap flag.

The app cache keeps every quick launch app, so its do-not-evict list
grows from 10 to 14.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
